(9/33)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">37.5 (12/32)</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;III (&#x00025;)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">30.0 (10/33)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">33.3 (11/32)</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;IV (&#x00025;)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.1 (8/33)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">25 (8/32)</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote1"><label/><p>HCC=hepatocellular carcinoma; HBsAg=hepatitis B surface antigen; HCV=hepatitis C virus; AST=aspartate transaminase; ICG R15=indocyanine green dye retention test at 15&#x02009;min; fc=capsular formation; fc-inf=tumour invasion to fc; vp=invasion to portal vein; vv=invasion to hepatic vein; b=invasion to bile duct; im=intrahepatic metastasis.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote2"><label>a</label><p>The low and high expression groups were determined by a median value of <italic>EZH2</italic> mRNA in the 66 tumour tissue specimens.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote3"><label>b</label><p>Histologic differentiation of the tumour.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>